CORE
inner.c
--pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.1\] line 14 static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: FAILURE$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The element size rows * columns overflows size_t and would wrap to 0, which a
one-byte object satisfies. The generated precondition rejects the overflow in
the runtime inner dimensions.
